# Keep GitHub's language bar describing the project, not its documentation.
#
# OVER_VIEW.html is 434KB, of which ~93% is the nine Mermaid diagrams
# pre-rendered to SVG and inlined so the page opens offline. Linguist ranks by
# bytes and counts inlined SVG as HTML, so that one file was reading as 55% of
# the repo — more than Rust and TypeScript combined.
#
# `linguist-documentation` (rather than `linguist-generated`) is deliberate:
# it drops the file from the language stats but keeps its diffs visible, and
# the ~30KB of page around the diagrams is hand-written and does get edited.
OVER_VIEW.html linguist-documentation

# The diagram sources are the thing to actually read; they're small, but they
# aren't project code either.
docs/diagrams/*.mmd linguist-documentation
